+native/tools/build_cycles_android.py (tools/rebase_build_tree.py does the work).
+It reads the old checkout root from CMakeCache.txt, moves the object folders
+CMake names after absolute source paths, rewrites the old root in every text
+file of the tree and in the referenced generated inputs under work/ (keeping
+their modification times), gives every referenced source, header, CMake file
+and library the modification time of the same file in the old checkout when
+the two are byte-identical (the old checkout must still exist; it is read
+only), then configures and builds as usual and checks that no build file still
+names the old root and that every compiled source is under this checkout.
+Files that differ from the old checkout rebuild, with everything that depends
+on them; an unchanged tree rebuilds nothing and produces byte-identical
+binaries. A copy that was already stale in the old checkout (objects older than
+their inputs there) rebuilds exactly what the old checkout would have rebuilt.
+Relinked binaries never match the old checkout byte for byte: CMake's build
+RUNPATH names the dependency prefix of the checkout that linked them. The
+overlay generator writes generated includes only when their content changes.
