+
+## Parity estimate (Step zero, 2026-10-22)
+
+Two figures, recomputed from the regenerated ledger and the source; both are
+reproducible with the method below. Neither is a release statement; the Metal
+binary on macOS remains the 100% reference.
+
+1. Ledger floor: reviewed rows with a tested status (isolated-, integrated- or
+   platform-tested, partial coverage, bounded evidence) divided by all 1,011
+   declaration rows (opcodes, closures, kernels, passes, modes, features,
+   tables). Today 109 of 1,011, **about 11%**: opcodes 61 of 111, closures 5 of
+   45, kernels 16 of 78, modes 27 of 621, passes, features and tables 0. It is a
+   floor: most rows (and every closure beyond the five reviewed families) have
+   not been reviewed, whatever the renderer implements. It rose from about 6%
+   because 48 texture, colour, utility, bump and derivative opcodes now have
+   reviews backed by current evidence instead of hand-edited statuses.
+2. Weighted implementation coverage: for the four behaviour families, the share
+   of functional rows (sentinels and category markers excluded) that the WebGPU
+   device implements and a reference-device gate exercises, read from the
+   source: opcodes decoded by the WGSL interpreter (`op_info` in
+   native/cycles/pipelines.cpp, plus `NODE_END`) 90 of 108 (83%); closures
+   handled by the WGSL closure code 15 of 41 (37%); device kernels the WebGPU
+   queue implements (native/cycles/queue.cpp) 22 of 77 (29%); passes written
+   by the renderer (Combined only) 1 of 56 (2%). Weights (an engineering
+   judgment, not a measurement): opcodes 25, closures 30, kernels 30, passes 15.
+   Result: **about 41%** (0.25 x 83 + 0.30 x 37 + 0.30 x 29 + 0.15 x 2).
+   Geometry (curves, points, subdivision, displacement), lighting beyond the
+   lamp set (environment importance sampling, light trees, linking), the film
+   and denoising stack and the platform matrix (three of nine RIDs with
+   reference-device evidence) sit outside these four families and are not in
+   this figure.
 
